1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
PortalPulse is a node-operations toolkit in development. This walkthrough uses real prototype snapshots, not a continuous recording.

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:23,000
The supplied synthetic facts are internally consistent. The report still says the current network is unverified and writes are prohibited.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Six stages keep their original facts and timestamps: identity, submission, inclusion, execution, finality, and state readback.

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Missing finality or readback stays unverified. A supplied execution failure stays abnormal; the failure reason is retained.

5
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:59,000
The digest detects content changes. It does not authenticate the source or prove consensus. All three verification flags remain false.

6
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Print acceptance covered five synthetic scenarios and 26 A4 pages. A 65-block ancestry fixture spans 14 pages, ending with readback and limits.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Next: confirm official V3 configuration and network identity, then use user-approved signing for the probe, exact execution, finality and readback.

8
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:32,000
Explore the public prototype and source. The Node Operations & Tooling project remains an offline prototype while official V3 integration is pending.
